============================================================================
H-B1 vs H-B2  Binding-head algebra comparison   (D=10240 = cubby-lm head)
============================================================================

[H-B3 corollary] cubby-lm VSABindingHead query is CONTINUOUS.
  cos(continuous query, sign(query))              = 0.798  (theory sqrt(2/pi)=0.798)
  argmax agreement, NO-signal (untrained) regime  = 17.6%  (worst case: argmax over pure crosstalk)
  top-1 = target, cos=0.55 signal, continuous q   = 100.0%
  top-1 = target, cos=0.55 signal, sign(q)        = 100.0%
  => in the OPERATING regime binarization is nearly lossless for readout.
  => H-B1's bipolar algebra needs a sign() step; H-B2's HRR does not.

[H-B1 vs H-B2] role-filler unbind from a superposition of n pairs
  (100-filler codebook; accuracy = correct filler is nearest)
  n pairs       1      3      5      8     12     20     40     80    160    320
  HRR        100   100   100   100   100   100   100   100   100   100   (%)
  BSC/MAP    100   100   100   100   100   100   100   100   100    97   (%)

[verdict]
  HRR  >=90%-recall capacity: n<= 320 pairs
  BSC  >=90%-recall capacity: n<= 320 pairs
  Both are viable; the deciding factor is the head's CONTINUOUS query:
  HRR unbinds it natively; BSC needs sign(), which is ~free in the signal regime.
